6.  handed to the field-theory lead: the static system whose constraint chain decides whether xi costs a degree of freedom
      (i)   nabla^2 Phi_N = 4 pi G rho_b
      (ii)  (1 - xi^2 nabla^2) Phi~ = Phi_N            [Helmholtz filter; the Gaussian used above is its smooth cousin]
      (iii) nabla^2 Phi = nabla . [ nu(|grad Phi~|/a_0) grad Phi~ ]
    Three elliptic equations, no time derivatives.  (ii) is what Theorem 8 localised into a dynamical field and killed;
    here it is a CONSTRAINT.  The question for the Dirac chain: with Phi~ a constrained variable, is the finite-k static
    block still 0 propagating DOF (as your two-field block was), and does the k -> 0 sector survive a background?
    Numbers to hold it to: xi >= 0.05 pc (the Saturn-orbit monopole bound, above the quadrupole's 0.03 pc; and NOT below ~0.03 pc, where smoothing makes the quadrupole worse); two regimes:
      small xi (0.05-0.1 pc): both Solar-System bounds pass, wide binaries keep part of the boost at 20-30 kAU with a knee near xi, globulars stay MOND (f13's +0.3 dex remains);
      large xi (~84 pc, from 3 of 4 globulars): Cassini passes, wide binaries Newtonian at all separations, dwarfs trimmed by 0.1-0.15 dex, discs untouched.
    Gaia DR4 binned in separation, and the outer-halo globulars, decide between them.

